in akron ohio the anger is rising and  these protesters say they will stay on  the streets until there's justice for 25  year old jalen walker who was shot dead  by police last monday  he was probably one of the most positive  people i ever came across in my whole  entire life  so when i first heard the news it was  like  i thought they got their names  officials say the incident began when  officers tried to stop walker for a  traffic violation  akron police say walker fired a gun at  officers who were chasing him after he  fled that he presented a threat to the  force  they plan to release body camera footage  later on sunday  [Music]  but a lawyer for the family says that  footage will show officers shot walker  dozens of times  some who've seen the video have  described it as graphic shocking even  barbaric  we really need to utilize the word keep  to peace  because when the people see what  is going to be shown in that footage  it's going to cause some problems and it  will go through nationwide  the shooting is the latest in a string  of police killings of black americans  that many say are unjustified  the 2020 murder of george floyd in  minneapolis ignited global protests  against racism and police brutality it's  the hypocrisy we have a problem with if  this was happening to everybody in our  community we would not care but it's not  happening to everybody  the officers involved in walker's  shooting have been placed on  administrative leave while an  investigation is underway  alexia o'brien al jazeera
 

